            Data: generics.ToHstore(map[string]string{}),
        },
    }
```

**File:** `services/ctl-api/internal/app/installs/service/create_install.go`

Update `CreateInstallV2Request.Validate()` (~line 29):
```go
// Old: if c.AWSAccount == nil && c.AzureAccount == nil {
// New:
accounts := 0
if c.AWSAccount != nil { accounts++ }
if c.AzureAccount != nil { accounts++ }
if c.GCPAccount != nil { accounts++ }
if accounts != 1 {
    return stderr.ErrUser{
        Description: "exactly one of aws_account, azure_account, or gcp_account must be provided",
        Err:         fmt.Errorf("exactly one cloud account must be provided"),
    }
}
```

Add GCP region validation (after the AWS region check):
```go
if c.GCPAccount != nil {
    if c.GCPAccount.Region == "" {
        return stderr.ErrUser{
            Description: "GCPAccount region is required",
            Err:         fmt.Errorf("GCPAccount region is required"),
        }
    }
}
```

Apply the same changes to `CreateInstallRequest.Validate()` (~line 136).

**Backwards compatibility:** The API now accepts `gcp_account` as a third option. Requests without it behave identically. The mutual-exclusivity check is stricter (exactly 1 instead of "at least 1 of aws/azure") which is also backwards-compatible since you could never successfully create an install with both before.

