### 3.4 OCI Registry — Google Artifact Registry
**File:** `pkg/plugins/configs/registry_oci.go`

Add type and field:
```go
OCIRegistryTypeGAR OCIRegistryType = "gar"
```
```go
GARAuth *gcpcredentials.Config `hcl:"gar_auth,block"`
```

**New package:** `bins/runner/internal/pkg/registry/gar/`

**`fetch.go`:**
```go
func FetchAccessInfo(ctx context.Context, cfg *configs.OCIRegistryRepository) (*registry.AccessInfo, error) {
    if cfg.OCIAuth != nil {
        // Use provided credentials directly (same pattern as ACR fallback)
        return &registry.AccessInfo{
            Image: cfg.Repository,
            Auth: &registry.AccessInfoAuth{
                Username:      cfg.OCIAuth.Username,
                Password:      cfg.OCIAuth.Password,
                ServerAddress: cfg.LoginServer,
            },
        }, nil
    }

    // Use Application Default Credentials to get an access token
    tokenSource, err := google.DefaultTokenSource(ctx, "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform")
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("unable to get default token source: %w", err)
    }
    token, err := tokenSource.Token()
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("unable to get token: %w", err)
    }

    return &registry.AccessInfo{
        Image: cfg.Repository,
        Auth: &registry.AccessInfoAuth{
            Username:      "oauth2accesstoken",
            Password:      token.AccessToken,
            ServerAddress: cfg.LoginServer,
        },
    }, nil
}
```

**File:** `bins/runner/internal/pkg/oci/repo.go`

Add case in `FetchAccessInfo` switch:
```go
case configs.OCIRegistryTypeGAR:
    accessInfo, err = gar.FetchAccessInfo(ctx, cfg)
```

### 3.5 Runner job integration
**File:** `bins/runner/internal/jobs/deploy/terraform/workspace.go`

Update the auth vars construction to include GCP:
```go
authVars, err := authvars.New(p.v,
    authvars.WithAWSAuth(p.state.plan.TerraformDeployPlan.AWSAuth),
    authvars.WithAzureAuth(p.state.plan.TerraformDeployPlan.AzureAuth),
    authvars.WithGCPAuth(p.state.plan.TerraformDeployPlan.GCPAuth),
)
```

Apply the same change to the sandbox terraform workspace:
**File:** `bins/runner/internal/jobs/sandbox/terraform/workspace.go`

### 3.6 Runner Dockerfile
**File:** `bins/runner/Dockerfile`

Add a build stage for `gke-gcloud-auth-plugin` (same pattern as kubelogin):
```dockerfile
FROM golang:1.25-alpine AS gke-auth-plugin

RUN apk add --update --no-cache curl ca-certificates
WORKDIR /bin
RUN curl -LO https://dl.google.com/dl/cloudsdk/channels/rapid/downloads/google-cloud-cli-linux-x86_64.tar.gz \
    && tar -xzf google-cloud-cli-linux-x86_64.tar.gz \
    && ./google-cloud-sdk/install.sh --quiet \
    && ./google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud components install gke-gcloud-auth-plugin --quiet \
    && cp ./google-cloud-sdk/bin/gke-gcloud-auth-plugin .
```

Add to final stage:
```dockerfile
COPY --from=gke-auth-plugin /bin/gke-gcloud-auth-plugin /usr/local/bin/gke-gcloud-auth-plugin
```

**Alternative (simpler):** Download the standalone binary directly:
```dockerfile
FROM golang:1.25-alpine AS gke-auth-plugin
RUN apk add --update --no-cache curl
RUN curl -Lo /usr/local/bin/gke-gcloud-auth-plugin \
    https://dl.k8s.io/release/v0.31.0/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl-gke-gcloud-auth-plugin \
    && chmod +x /usr/local/bin/gke-gcloud-auth-plugin
```

The exact approach depends on the distribution method Google uses at the time of implementation. The key requirement is that `gke-gcloud-auth-plugin` is available on `$PATH` in the runner container.

---

## Backwards Compatibility Summary

| Change | Impact on existing AWS/Azure installs |
|--------|--------------------------------------|
| New `CloudPlatformGCP` constant | None — string enum, additive |
| New `GCPAccount` model + table | None — new table, no schema changes to existing tables |
| New `GCPAccount` pointer on Install | None — nullable, `nil` for all existing installs |
| New `AppRunnerTypeGCP` | None — additive string constant |
| New `GCPStackOutputs` | None — new nullable pointer on `InstallStackOutputs` |
| New `GCPCloudAccount` on state | None — nullable, `nil` for existing states |
| Validation change (exactly 1 account) | Compatible — was already impossible to send both aws+azure |
| `getAuth()` 4 return values | Internal-only function — all callers updated in this PR |
| `GCPAuth` on plan types | None — nullable JSON field, absent in existing plans |
| GCP proto message | Additive — new field number 3 on `InstallContext` |
| `OCIRegistryTypeGAR` | None — new constant, new switch case |
| `WithGCPAuth()` option | None — new option, existing calls don't use it |
| `gke-gcloud-auth-plugin` in Dockerfile | None — additive binary, doesn't affect existing tools |

**No existing behavior is changed.** All GCP code paths are reachable only when an install is created with `gcp_account` or when `AppRunnerTypeGCP` is configured on an app.

